# =====================================================================
# Release V017 -- Bronze: one Process_Config job per table
# =====================================================================
# Collapses the Bronze metadata from 248 per-tenant rows (BRONZE_T{tid}_{ENTITY})
# to 31 per-table rows (BRONZE_{ENTITY}). The tenant + full-refresh are supplied at
# RUNTIME: Audit.ETL_Run_Process gains optional @Tenant_ID/@Full_Refresh and resolves
# {TID}/{FR} tokens in Process_Parameters, so one config row serves every tenant.
# Execution stays per-tenant (Audit.usp_Load_Bronze is still called once per tenant by
# Orchestrate_Bronze, tied to each async Dentally extract) and per-tenant audit
# granularity is preserved (Process_Execution_Log records the resolved @Tenant_ID).
#
# Backward-compatible: Silver/Gold config rows have no tokens and callers pass no
# tenant, so token resolution is a no-op -- Silver/Gold are untouched.
#
# usp_Rerun_Failed_Jobs is updated: it can no longer match Process_Options to the
# (now templated) Process_Parameters, so it seeds by Process_Name (1:1 with code),
# captures the failed run's resolved options (Rerun_Plan.Failed_Options) and re-runs
# the correct tenant by parsing @Tenant_ID/@Full_Refresh back out.
#
# Data is unchanged (this is orchestration metadata only) -> NO regression re-baseline.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V017__bronze_one_job_per_table.manifest
#      (set $env:FABRIC_SERVER for prod)
# =====================================================================

# --- Audit objects ---
DEPLOY  Fabric\Audit.Rerun_Plan.Table.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Audit.ETL_Run_Process.StoredProcedure.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Audit.usp_Rerun_Failed_Jobs.StoredProcedure.sql

# --- Bronze orchestrator ---
DEPLOY  Fabric\Audit.usp_Load_Bronze.StoredProcedure.sql

# --- Re-seed metadata (idempotent DELETE + INSERT) ---
DEPLOY  Fabric\Audit.Process_Config.Data.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Audit.Process_Dependency.Data.sql
